## 16. Priority boundary

The following are **not** claimed as new here:

- the profile-pairing identity for counting from already-constructed histograms;
- the Walsh-Hadamard transform used to accelerate profile pairing;
- low-order marginal/Fourier equivalence;
- generic partial materialization of low-dimensional data-cube aggregates.

A bounded 2026-09-28 search found related exact/approximate data-cube materialization and factorized-aggregation literature, but did not locate this exact combination of (i) fixed-cut GF(2) factor profiles, (ii) profile-indexed coordinate moments and character moments, (iii) the cumulative destructive-update recurrence, and (iv) the stated gauge-invariant lifecycle bounds. That absence is **not** evidence of firstness. The contribution status remains **apparently differentiated combination/corollary; exact priority unresolved** pending specialist search.
